 {:seon.task/name "a-running-fibers-dump-shows-its-current-frames"
  :seon.task/plan "Found 2026-10-27 (the turn-0 hang, task seon.agent/a-turn-0-prove-does-not-walk-the-checkout): seon's fiber dump (kill -INFO) of a process whose only fiber is running answers 'running fiber, no saved continuation' and names nothing, so the one process that burned 175e9 ticks could not be located in code; its native sample showed only getcwd and directory listing. A running fiber's current frames must be in the dump (Jolt's runtime: the fiber's own stack at the signal, as a parked fiber's saved continuation shows), so the dump of a spinning process names the Clojure function it is in. Belongs to Jolt (a jolt/<topic> branch, AGENTS section 1); owner jolt-compare. Proof: a process spinning in a known function (a loop in a test fixture) dumps that function under its running fiber."
