 {:seon.task/name "a-test-child-starts-as-a-test-runner-does"
  :seon.task/plan "Seen 2026-11-02 by the context lab's curation pilot (a scripted replay on a reverse-patched tree; report in /private/tmp/seon-l2r/618a903ed3/tree/target/curated-turn-5.edn): the agent's prove passed its proof but 13 reached tests failed and 3 errored in its test child, all green under bin/test in the same tree, so the run parked :waiting and no change near seon.ctx, seon.repl or seon.db could end green. Three causes: (1) root's interrupt pending in the agent when the turn's observe forked its test child (it is cleared only when the turn's evals begin, seon.turn/act!), so every eval in the child answered \"interrupted by root\"; (2) the child kept the agent's live page walk, whose reactions answered a test's swap! of ctx (seon.ctx-test/a-swap-costs-what-it-changed 128 calls against 113); (3) seon.db-test's corpus read docs/ relative to the working directory, which in a test child is its own run directory. Correct: a test child starts as bin/test's runner does, its interrupt state cleared (seon.intr/forked!), proven; a test reads the checkout's files by (seon.config/checkout). Cause (2) is unconfirmed: a child forked from inside an eval held no walk (seon.agent-test/a-test-child-starts-as-a-test-runner-does), so the cost overrun is reproduced from the pilot's report before anything is changed for it."
  :seon.task/kind :work
  :seon.task/proofs #{seon.agent-test/a-test-child-starts-as-a-test-runner-does}}
 {:seon.task/name "the-done-rule-holds-under-load"
  :seon.task/plan "Seen 2026-11-02 in the optimization session's bin/prove --merge of jolt/one-search at load 15-19 (logs target/prove/20261102T110219-57930/shard-2.log): seon.agent-test/a-task-whose-proofs-pass-is-done-only-when-what-it-reaches-is-green answered [:green :merged []], the change that breaks main's edit test merged with no reason named; the same test alone at load ~8 is green (refused, the stray red named). In the same run seon.agent-test/an-agents-first-search-reads-the-index-it-inherited measured a first grep 9.07 MB against a second 2.38 MB (green alone): seon.profile/alloc-bytes counts the whole process, so a fiber working beside the measured call is counted. Cause of the first not yet known. Ruled out 2026-11-02: the stall bound (the test with :seon.config.agent/stall-ms 1 at load 12 still refused the change, green). Left: a verdict reused from the shared verdict cache (target/results) at a digest the agent's change should have moved, or a reached test the agent's run never ran under load (its test child's ceiling, a test plan that changed); the next look reads that run's store (its root's runs dir) before the test's tree is removed. Correct: whatever the load, a reached test the change breaks is named and the task does not merge (no clock decides: AGENTS 4); a cost test measures its own call's allocation, or reads no fiber's beside it."
