  :seon.task/proofs #{seon.agent-test/a-task-whose-proofs-pass-is-done-only-when-what-it-reaches-is-green}}
 {:seon.task/name "the-agents-state-is-declared"
  :seon.task/plan "The owner, 2026-11-03, on the bug-class audit read at c200a44aa9: \"make sure all of this fixes are applied and the docs are updated\"; by AGENTS section 3 step 4 its report says what allowed the class, why the change makes it impossible, and which siblings it checked. What exists: seon.agent/state is one mutable map, its keys described in a comment, its schema the tag :seon.agent/state [:map], with about 62 swap!/reset! sites and no validator (the one set-validator! in src is seon.ctx's). Nothing declares which keys an eval may replace, which survive a fork or which a test child resets, and four fixes were this class: d1ab45ec12 and 24b5508112 (socket and intake reader lost when state was replaced, moved by hand to link), c4a4cdd495 and 2c3867e897 (a test child inherited the interrupt and the page walk, reset by hand at one fork site), 42854c8c33 (a carry read :db from state). The change: :seon.agent/state a closed map with each key's type and a per-key property (:seon.agent/on-fork :reset or :keep); set-validator! from it while contracts are on; the forked child's state derived from the schema in place of the hand dissoc and resets; host handles stay out (in link). Check seon.intr's stack and pending atoms the same way. Docs: docs/agent.md."
