 {:seon.task/name "a-refused-exit-watch-is-an-answer"
  :seon.task/plan "Seen 2026-11-04 in bin/check scale at 100 agents (target/check run of branch jolt/an-evals-record-has-its-shape, 76ab975c96): one agent's test child failed with `jolt.io-poller/exit-chan: kevent refused the watch`, ex-data {:pid 4300 :errno 35} (EAGAIN), thrown at jolt/io_poller.clj:1139 under seon.agent/read-to-exit, and went on as `Exception in go/fiber body (channel closed)`: :every-eval-and-test-passed false, 99 of 100 ok. What allowed it: an outside-world failure point (a kernel watch on a child) that throws in a fiber instead of answering, against AGENTS section 4 (a wait ends with its value or a typed error). Correct: find what EAGAIN means for EVFILT_PROC at that moment (Jolt's io poller; the fix is there, on a jolt/<topic> branch, with its gates): retried by what the kernel says, or the exit read another way; and a watch the kernel keeps refusing answers the waiter as an error value the test child reports. Named in docs/failure-points.md with its edge function."
