 {:seon.task/name "a-proof-child-that-died-says-why"
  :seon.task/plan "What was seen: seon.agent-test/a-two-child-proof-run-ends-with-its-agent red once in bin/prove --merge at 2672c71fdc (2026-11-04, target/prove/20261104T130554-11760, shard-1, machine load about 6): began [49 -1], child B's fifo closed with no byte written, before the test killed the agent. The same test at the same digest: green three times alone, and it had been green before. The change under proof (seon.render/one-way-to-make-what-an-agent-is-sent, step 2) touches no test child or fifo. What this means: a writer opened the fifo (the reader's open returned) and closed it without its write, so child B died or returned between the FileOutputStream and its write, or its open was not child B's. Inferred, not shown: nothing kept child B's stderr or exit. What should be true: a proof child's death in a run says why (AGENTS 4, nothing crashes and nothing hangs), so the next red names its cause; then the cause is fixed. Proof: the test, under load, keeps what child B said and how it ended."
  :seon.task/kind :work
